{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"03fdf8b976074d85","type":"group","x":-640,"y":-520,"width":1000,"height":615,"label":"Hopekirk Worldbuilding"},
		{"id":"c8445e5b90bbd654","type":"text","text":"## Sandals\nA jolly cobbler named Sandals appears on the road. He boasts, “Hopkirks buying up my shoes faster than I can cobble ‘em together!” He hears music inside, but he’s never been let in. “Come to think of it, nobody comes out…” \n\n**Reward:**\nHe knows a bit about the village layout.","x":-1698,"y":-21,"width":327,"height":334,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"43a610acfce63248","type":"text","text":"## Bandits\n\nTwo bandits are caught plundering an abandoned carriage. They appear too lovestruck to fight, gladly handing over pilfered riches as one proposes to the other. \n\nHeroes receive a wedding invitation.\n\nDC 16 Insight Check: Their excitement borders on desperation.","x":-1698,"y":-361,"width":327,"height":334},
		{"id":"966039da86c8afe0","type":"text","text":"# Random Encounters","x":-1684,"y":-560,"width":300,"height":120,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"fb723f5401d8c28a","type":"text","text":"# Quest hook\nHopkirk’s exports have ceased. The heroes’ favorite inn is low on food & drink\nThe owner requests aid in tracing missed deliveries, promising to name a dish after them on their return.","x":-2360,"y":17,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"06502ffe53bbb2c5","type":"text","text":"# The Emerald Vow\n\nCrash the perfect wedding in this whimsical fae-inspired Nimble adventure!\n\n**Synopsis:**\nThe charming village of Hopkirk rejoiced when their very own Merrin and Drayna were betrothed. When Drayna’s extended Fae family arrived, the locals gladly embraced their promise of “the perfect wedding!” At first, it was delightful. Music filled the streets, tables overflowed with food, and laughter rang day and night. But days became weeks, and the celebration didn’t end. Sleep was scorned, fields went untended, children wandered in a daze of sweets and song. The in-laws have co-opted the wedding with vows of their own — a ritual to summon their patron, the Emerald Bride. Should she be called, she will bind the mortal realm into her dominion: an endless festival where every moment is dance and delight… until joy burns to frenzy, bodies collapse from exhaustion, and reality frays beneath unceasing merriment. Now, with the happy couple missing, and the villagers wilting beneath the suffocating cheer of their Fey guests, one thing is clear: someone HAS to stop this wedding.\n\n---\n**Was ist das?** Wir spielen einen NimbleV2 Oneshot. Keine Ahnung was das ist? Kein problem. Nimble ist ein Tabletop Roleplaying System ähnlich zu Dungeons & Dragons oder Das schwarze Auge.\n\n**Wie lange spielen wir?** Wir spielen eure Geschichte in einem Oneshot. Es ist also nicht klar wie und was genau passiert. Erfahrungs gemäß dauert das ganze ca. 4 stunden, die ihr auch bitte einplanen solltet.\n\n**Was braucht ihr?** Bringt etwas spaß und Energie mit! Ich erkläre das system und bringe alle Ressourcen mit die wir am Abend brauchen. Falls ihr welche habt, bringt euren Lieblingsstift und/oder Lieblingswürfel mit!\n\n**Welche Sprache ist das?** Wir spielen ein Englishes modul und auch das system is auf english. Wir spielen auf Deutsch und ich helfe euch alles zu verstehen. \n\n4-5 Spieler\n\n**Trigger Warnings:** Mind Control, Exhaustion, the food may eat you.","x":-3140,"y":-100,"width":680,"height":880,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"3e89fb4c0e88730e","type":"text","text":"## Crows\n**PREQ:** Druid\n \n Birds decorate scarecrows with flowers, cawing away in seeming celebration. If a hero can speak to animals: “Happy Couple!”, “Emerald Bride!”. If disturbed, they fly off to the Manor on Hopkirk’s hill.","x":-1698,"y":340,"width":314,"height":293},
		{"id":"1aab359df2b0bc02","type":"text","text":"Hamlet is seemingly abandoned. Wedding invites scattered about, stuffed under doors.","x":-160,"y":-508,"width":270,"height":116},
		{"id":"8862a7107459a4d2","type":"text","text":"**Hollow Hamlet.** Outside the village palisades, empty farmsteads. Doors hang open, carts litter the street.","x":-569,"y":-508,"width":250,"height":116},
		{"id":"2c8e630284fb6191","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20250929212116.png","x":-360,"y":-1520,"width":528,"height":875},
		{"id":"94fd9074607a221a","type":"text","text":"# **The Rambling Cat** \nCharming tavern, garlands, holly, roaring fire. The festivities of the street flow in and out.\n\nPeople APPEAR cheerful but are miserable in reality. ","x":813,"y":553,"width":327,"height":247,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2cca589a161bb438","type":"text","text":"### Rumors\n\n• “Merrin knew she was half-Fae; he’s cursed us all!” \n• “His In-Laws hold us hostage; how can we drive them away?”\n• “Keep smiling or they’ll toss you into their arena!\n• “The bride brought this plague on us— Someone needs to find her…","x":500,"y":920,"width":313,"height":380},
		{"id":"b1a6b80bc9a81459","type":"text","text":"### Pie for pie\nA boisterous, rotund attendee **Saffron** calls out for challengers: “Who can out-eat me?” Pies and meat pile up before him. \n\nBest of 3 Strength Check against his roll (+5, a Dwarf can reroll 1 failure). \n\nHappy villagers also participate, but fail. \n\n**On success:** gifted a Challenger’s Stein. \n**On failure**, poisoned for 1 hour.","x":-135,"y":680,"width":440,"height":340},
		{"id":"4db9671a81d600da","type":"text","text":"**What’s with the guests?** \nThey’re TOO happy. Tired smiles, bloodshot eyes; dirt-caked and blistered feet— their feverous celebration is involuntary. \n\n**(DC 14 Insight:** Not everyone. While some guests are cursed, others are acting. The Innkeeper (Lyra) in particular is carefully watching you and the in-laws who seem to not be from Hopkirk, their unending joy is genuine.","x":460,"y":200,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"6c6f31d72bf8f549","type":"text","text":"**Champion’s Stein.** (1/safe rest) drink out of it and make a STR save (with disadvantage) gain temp HP equal to the result.","x":-68,"y":1100,"width":307,"height":157},
		{"id":"0e6d5ba4b53228a9","type":"text","text":"### Dance off\nA lithe attendee **Sundew** likewise invites a hero: “Who can out-dance me?” She twirls endlessly. \n\nBest of 3 DEX check against her roll (+7, a Zephyr can reroll 1 failure). \n\n**On success:** gifted a Dancer’s Rose. \n\n**On failure,** take 1d10 damage as you twirl into a stack of glasses. \n\nVillagers also participate, but fail.","x":-605,"y":680,"width":440,"height":340},
		{"id":"1797444cfbbe24e7","type":"text","text":"**Dancer’s Rose.** While Dying, you may make DEX save (instead of STR) to act without taking a Wound.","x":-569,"y":1100,"width":368,"height":157},
		{"id":"9525f4f89e6fa2f6","type":"text","text":"Farm animals roam free, collecting decorations for their pens, trailing ribbons. DC 12 Perception: Jew- elry among the detritus (50gp)!","x":20,"y":-306,"width":296,"height":157},
		{"id":"b1961d159b45cce1","type":"text","text":"# Hopkirk (Worldbuilding)\n","x":-480,"y":-268,"width":265,"height":135,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b746d07e7723b2a7","type":"text","text":"Lyra to the rescue (if everyone is bewitched)","x":140,"y":468,"width":251,"height":85},
		{"id":"eefd808cd0fd427f","type":"text","text":"# Hopkirk (Challenges)\n","x":-298,"y":440,"width":265,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"21b5c289ec72c726","type":"text","text":"**Bewitched Festivities.** Any hero who dances or partakes in food must make a DC 13 WIL save, or become overtaken with a festive urge to eat, drink, dance (lasts until harmed—a slap will do).","x":-372,"y":200,"width":414,"height":134},
		{"id":"bc8cb66b22e0f0b2","type":"text","text":"**Green Street.** Maypoles and flowers surround an out- door banquet - People dance, laugh and feast endlessly.","x":-507,"y":-33,"width":334,"height":100},
		{"id":"5df02e06acb492a9","type":"text","text":"### Invitation\nThere is an emerald green letterbox on it that says: “Invited guests only!” and opens its “mouth” (Access with invitation)","x":-1154,"y":640,"width":316,"height":187,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"3a6926dc02a2677e","type":"text","text":"Invitation sources\n- search nearby houses/farmsteads\n- receive one from sandals","x":-1141,"y":340,"width":290,"height":200},
		{"id":"9e537cdbf26e704e","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20250929210639.png","x":-1276,"y":917,"width":561,"height":210,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"249131db428087e5","type":"text","text":"### Drawbridge\nThere is an emerald green letterbox on it that says: “Invited guests only!” and opens its “mouth” (Access with invitation)","x":-1154,"y":53,"width":316,"height":187,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"03409946c5020065","type":"text","text":"### Challenge(s)","x":-1098,"y":-100,"width":181,"height":73,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"500d9c468da6d9b8","x":575,"y":40,"width":285,"height":103,"type":"text","text":"The food is bewitched and will make you crazy to party endlessly"},
		{"id":"a53723a4bb94b478","type":"text","text":"**Bard:**\nBlood and twine, thistle-and-thyme Dress of sage and hair of wine Pale of skin and verdant-eyed We tremble at the Emerald Bride!\n\nDC 16 Lore or Songweaver\nA tale of an obscure Fae deity, linked to endless revelry. Her entering the mundane world would be disastrous.","x":852,"y":960,"width":308,"height":340},
		{"id":"6edca7226e5bd909","type":"text","text":"# Cellar \n\"Come quietly\"\n\nIron horseshoes are hung, salt at the threshold \"Mind the charms, keeps them from snooping\"\n\nShoes are piled high, people try to recover from the party outside.\na women is taught a dance but she can barely stand.\n\nLyra explains that the fae are extended family of Draynas; Festive prison; \n\nDissenters are brough to the Manor or the Arena;\n\n\"Please free the people in the Manor, we are running out of safe food\"\n\nThe bride and groom are missing\n","x":1260,"y":473,"width":520,"height":467,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"debdc5330036c895","x":1240,"y":1027,"width":411,"height":207,"type":"text","text":" The groom’s mother is among the crowd. She pleads her son’s innocence: “He must be enchanted by Drayna.” (false). She begs for his freedom. She carries a portrait of the betrothed. DC 10 Insight: Drayna has amber skin and brown eyes, not the Emerald Bride of Tafeo’s lyrics!"},
		{"id":"3693481942e4bace","type":"text","text":"# Backstreet \nTransformed into a fancy garden party\n\n\"The staff has arrived\"\nroll 1d6\n1. Braid my hair wont you (a man of snakes)\n2. She isnt speaking to me (she is imaginary)\n3. Play me a tune (a lute without strings)\n4. Feed my pet\n5. This Bogey took my seat (8ft tall hair monster, hunched in a small chair)\n6. Pour me a cup of tea! (the teapot is comically large and inconceivably heavy.)\n\nThe arena and a tournament is mentioned in conversation.\n","x":1920,"y":473,"width":520,"height":467,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"6030ab3cf5d654ca","type":"text","text":"# Manor\nAutumn foliage. Many birdcages, stacks of scrolls, filled with drafted wedding vows. \n\n- birds mimic voice stolen from around Hopkirk, including snippets of the heroes conversations\n- The \"vows\" DC 14 Arcana: Not vows but a summoning spell in the works \n\t- With this ring we are thine\n\t  Bound in shadow and shine\n\t  for better, for best, forever we cry,\n\t  Step through the veil, O Emerald Bride.\n- in the garden a gremlin writes invitations and does not talk to the party, a ready invitation is given to a raven and send away","x":2580,"y":473,"width":520,"height":467,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"2b371df38fbee0e2","x":3149,"y":817,"width":391,"height":323,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"Manors kitchen\n\nA cramped mess of icing and ribbons\n\nFey cooks dash about, a cake is on the loose!\nBewitched utensisls (2/hero) and a bewitched Cake attack\n\nSwollen mice lie nearby, surrounded by crumbs of cheese, lazily cheering the partys victory"},
		{"id":"823314c281794681","x":3149,"y":473,"width":391,"height":307,"color":"3","type":"text","text":"Manors Guestroom\n\nFashioned into a makeshift prison\nhundreds of keys are strewn about, the people are trying to escape.\n\nMr. Pampo has forged the prison and the rune inscribed wedding rings, promised he could rejoin his family, the rings purpose is unkown but they are important.\n\nGuides villagers back to the Inn"},
		{"id":"a722cf935ce5507f","x":3175,"y":1220,"width":300,"height":323,"color":"3","type":"text","text":"Arla, a apprentice baker is locked in the pantry.\nShe shares a healing potion and a few cookies (10hp)\n\nFind my father Pampo- he refused to celebrate, he will know how to break everyone out. "},
		{"id":"b72c8b9708b42068","x":3640,"y":560,"width":608,"height":514,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"# Hopkirk Chapel\n\nA wedding ceremony frozen in time.\n- the betrothed couple stand in a circle of runes frozen in time. Behind the altar, the fae aunt &Uncle preside over an ongoing ritual. A portal has opened and the emerald bride is slowly emerging\n- If the rings are removed (action) the betrothed spring into action.\nBIG SHOWDOWN"}
	],
